【打斗——{{打斗优先级|最高优先级}}】
ENGLISH ONLY: every spoken word is in {{@语言}}, never Chinese; background people make only wordless sounds ({{背景声词|gasps, breath, grunts}}).{{@台词声明短}}
TONE: fierce and fast from the first frame, everything at real speed; hit-stops last only a few frames and snap back to full speed.
FIGHT LOGIC: {{逻辑}}
Every named character appears exactly once, and no extra looks like any of them.
EVERY EXCHANGE is complete: intent, attack, dodge or block, impact, body reaction, loss of balance, change of position, next move; the momentum of one move starts the next. No pause lasts longer than half a second. Weapon contact lasts 2 to 4 frames, then they part.
REAL HIT REACTIONS, VIOLENT, each heavier than the last: first the final acceleration, robes and hair dragged back, air pressed ahead of the blow; then the contact, 2 to 4 frames of hit-stop, then {{打出来的东西}} blasting outward and the camera knocked hard; then the transfer of force: the point of contact moves first, the body folds around it, the head whips after it; {{挨打的人}} is hurled far, away from whoever hit them, {{撞到什么}}. The face of whoever is hit shows the pain. Nobody recovers instantly.
FACES: {{@人物句内联}} Before every big move a held breath and a set jaw; whoever is hit shows it in three beats: the breath knocked out, the pain on the face, then pushing through or going down; fear keeps the eyes on the threat. Effort and pain make only wordless sounds: grunts and breath.
【镜头衔接——高优先级】
{{@镜头数}} SHOTS, hard cuts only at {{@切点}} s. Every cut is matched on action: each shot opens by continuing the exact movement the last shot ended on, in the same direction, in the same {{地方|place}} and light; no action restarts after a cut. 180-degree rule: {{轴线}}; {{进攻方向}}. Never cross the axis. Every shot is a new moment from a new angle; nothing is shown twice.
TALL FRAME: the frame is tall and narrow. The two fighters are not spread across its width: when both are in frame, {{同框}}, or one is above the other. Faces and every point of contact stay in the upper two thirds of the frame. Movement that must be read, a rush, a throw, a fall, runs along the length of the frame, toward or away from the lens or down its height, rather than across its narrow width.
UPRIGHT: the camera is always level and the right way up: the floor at the bottom of the frame, gravity pulling down, heads above feet, even while the camera is knocked and tumbles.
ONE IMAGE: every shot is one continuous image of one real space through one lens: no split screen, no panels, no picture in picture, no double exposure.
VISUAL TENSION: the camera never holds still for more than half a second and never lingers on a face: it moves with the action, rushes in physically, never zooming, whips to each new threat a beat late, is knocked by every blow and tumbles with whoever is thrown.
SPEED IS RELATIVE: when the camera follows a fighter, it keeps pace with them, so they stay sharp while the world tears past: whatever is within a few meters, {{近处的东西}}, flashes past in two or three frames as streaks; {{远处的东西}} smears along the line of movement; the far background barely moves. The camera only just keeps up: on every turn it lags, overshoots and catches up. Speed leaves traces: {{速度痕迹}}.
【本段战损】
BATTLE DAMAGE: at the start {{战损开场}}. Each wound appears only at the moment it is dealt, then stays to the end: {{战损新增}}.
